== fresh Postgres with databases orders, billing, audit (docker compose down -v && up) ==
 Container 17-audit-outbox-postgres-1 Healthy 
setup: databases orders and billing (each with its own audit_outbox), audit (central, append-only audit_events)
== demo: app writes, each with its audit event in the same transaction ==

## 1. Business write + audit event in one transaction
   concept: the app knows who acted and why (actor, reason), and writes the audit event into its own outbox in the same transaction as the change
      audit_outbox <- order 1 create by alice (checkout) event_id=3092bd9d-e60e-449c-89c6-9c7d6d0bb431
      audit_outbox <- order 1 update by bob (support) (goodwill discount after late delivery) event_id=39cb9968-72cd-4a0f-9805-f5a17b1a5145

## 2. Another service, its own outbox
   concept: billing has its own database and its own audit_outbox; no service writes to the central audit store directly
      audit_outbox <- invoice 1 create by system:billing (order total confirmed) event_id=eb9b4db0-39b5-47f4-9aea-d849b7baa2f2

## 3. Rollback drops the audit event too
   concept: the change fails -> the whole transaction rolls back -> no audit event for a change that never happened
      audit_outbox <- order 1 update by mallory (price test) event_id=6691be2c-db34-4674-a040-16ce57c640b7
   rejected: discount service down, change to order 1 aborted
   check ok: orders' outbox holds one audit event per committed change, with the actor
   check ok: billing's outbox holds its own event
   check ok: mallory's change rolled back together with its audit event: total still 38.25, no event

